<title>FRANCE: State of Bavaria buys nine Eurocopter helicopters.</title>
<headline>State of Bavaria buys nine Eurocopter helicopters.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German Bavarian state interior ministry has signed a 60 million mark contract for nine Eurocopter EC 135 helicopters for its police squadron, the Franco-German helicopter maker said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The EC 135 is a light, twin-engine aircraft which can carry up to eight people. The Bavarian order is the biggest single order for the aircraft, which is the latest product in the Eurocopter range, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Eurocopter is a joint venture between French state-owned SNI Aerospatiale and Daimler-Benz Aerospace AG.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 pnt</p>
